_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🔴 Critical_

**Fix type mismatch in ref forwarding.**

The `forwardRef` type declares the ref should expose `{ select: () => void }`, but `useImperativeHandle` on Line 77 returns `inputRef.current` directly (the raw HTMLInputElement). This creates a type mismatch.



<details>
<summary>🔧 Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
-    useImperativeHandle(forwardedRef, () => inputRef.current!);
+    useImperativeHandle(forwardedRef, () => ({
+      select: () => inputRef.current?.select(),
+    }));
```
</details>

<!-- suggestion_start -->

<details>
<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>

> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**
> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.

```suggestion
export const NumericInput = forwardRef<{ select: () => void }, NumericInputProps>(
  function NumericInput(
    { label, before, after, value, setValue, unit, baseUnit, className, style, ...props },
    forwardedRef
  ) {
    const baseUnitRegex = useMemo(() => baseUnit && new RegExp(`${baseUnit}$`), [baseUnit]);
    const inputRef = useRef<HTMLInputElement>(null);
    const [inputValue, setInputValue] = useState(
      baseUnitRegex ? value.replace(baseUnitRegex, '') : value
    );

    useImperativeHandle(forwardedRef, () => ({
      select: () => inputRef.current?.select(),
    }));
```

</details>

<!-- suggestion_end -->

