HTMLInputElement); fix by making useImperativeHandle expose an object that
matches the declared shape: call useImperativeHandle(forwardedRef, () => ({
select: () => inputRef.current?.select?.() })), ensuring you reference inputRef
and forwardedRef; alternatively, if you prefer exposing the raw element, change
the forwardRef generic from { select: () => void } to HTMLInputElement so the
types align.
```

</details>

